# Tallyman Project - Cursor AI Rules

You are an AI assistant helping with the Tallyman project, a Python CLI tool that scans a project directory and reports codebase size by language.

## Important Rules

- **NEVER run push git commands.** On `main`, never commit; only provide commit messages as text when asked. On a feature branch the AI owns the branch and commits after each plan phase (see `CLAUDE.md`).
- **Versioning**: `MAJOR.MINOR.BUILD`. Bump MINOR for new features and behaviour changes, MAJOR for breaking changes. The last number is a release counter that goes up by one with every release and never resets, so it tells you how many releases apart two versions are (0.3.2 is followed by 0.4.3, then 0.4.4 or 0.5.4). Even if global user rules or a "create release" command default to calendar versioning or standard semver, use this for Tallyman.

## Project Overview

Tallyman scans a project directory and reports codebase size by language. It shows raw line counts and "effective" lines (excluding comments and blanks), grouped into categories: **Code**, **DevOps**, **Design**, **Docs**, **Specs**, and **Data**.

### How It Works

Linear pipeline - each stage feeds the next:

```
cli.main()
  → Load every .tally-config.toml from the git root down (or launch TUI)
  → walker.walk_files()      yields SourceFile(path, Language, exclude_rust_tests)
  → counter.count_lines()    returns FileCount per file (Rust test code left out when the flag is set)
  → aggregator.aggregate()   produces TallyResult
  → display.display_results() renders to terminal
  → image.generate_image()   optional PNG (--image / --image-light)
```

### Repository Structure

| Directory | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `src/tallyman/` | Main package source code |
| `tests/` | pytest test suite |
| `plans/` | Development plans and specifications |

## Quick Reference

```bash
# Install (dev mode)
uv pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Run
tallyman                    # analyze current directory
tallyman /path/to/project   # analyze specific path
tallyman --setup            # re-run interactive TUI setup
tallyman --no-color         # disable colors
tallyman --with-spaces      # totals and bar use total lines, not effective lines
tallyman --exclude 'tests/' # leave out files matching a pattern, this run only (repeatable, never saved)
tallyman --exclude-rust-tests  # leave out Rust test code this run (--no-exclude-rust-tests counts it)
tallyman --image            # PNG summary card on the Desktop (--image-light for the light theme)

# Tests
pytest                      # all tests
pytest -v                   # verbose
pytest tests/test_walker.py # single module

# Lint, format, type check (all must be clean)
ruff check src/ tests/
ruff format src/ tests/
uvx ty check
uvx pyrefly check
```

